 [{:phase :offline-source :description "Construct isolated test-only actor, explicit operator, fake authenticated transport, private owner, deterministic faultable durable store and fresh direct buffers; fake objects exercise protocol only and never prove actual Axxium, GovOne, storage or native transport qualification."}
  {:case :binding :assert "Reject forged actor/context/grant, wrong authenticated peer, actor/session substitution, admin bypass, wrong operation/scope/resource/incarnation/epoch/revision/range/bytes/contract/destination, mutable copies, duplicate fields and expired approvals; bound read and replace each positive-control separately."}
  {:case :owner :assert "Only explicit grant and agent-owned registered object succeed; reject same-name recreated object, indirect/shared aliases, alias created during operation, hooks/overlays, reentrancy, concurrent writers, stale revision, invalid UTF-8 boundaries, oversize and untrusted callbacks. Assert zero disclosure or mutation on each denial."}
  {:case :order :assert "Deterministically interleave revoke before, concurrent with, and after commit/release, including ACK and persistence barriers. Observe owner order, count actual mutation entries and output bytes; acknowledged-before must have zero effect, after cannot retroactively undo. Two contenders sharing a grant admit at most one attempt. Include identity invalidation and policy-update barriers only when those owner integrations exist; otherwise explicitly mark them blocked."}
  {:case :faults :assert "Inject persistence write/fsync failures, corrupt or truncated recovery, rollback, duplicate owner, clock faults, disconnect, stale generation, failure after consume, partial delete/insert, crash/restart and lost reply. No failed revoke is ACKed; old grants never revive; no automatic retry; indeterminate outcomes remain indeterminate. Test durable adapter against its real specified persistence later, not only a fake."}
  {:case :governance :assert "Deny missing/unavailable/stale GovOne decision, wrong destination and policy change before release; verify no bytes escape. Synthetic policy doubles do not prove real GovOne admission or change ordering."}
  {:phase :future-separately-permitted :description "After exact-source independent review and real identity, storage, exclusion, policy, host ingress and native ordering proofs, obtain an explicit effect permit naming exact binary/source hashes, endpoint and server generation, isolated authenticated test actor, freshly created agent-owned fixtures, permitted operations, bounds, observation and cleanup. Then run real-owner tests for exact bytes and actual mutation counts, including same-name replacement and disconnect/restart only if separately permitted. Existing emacs.service is not automatically selected or authorized; no live buffers, loading, server, socket or restart in this phase of work."}]
